# Begin with the End in Mind: Final Project Overview

Unit 6 is the Semester 2 capstone, where students design and build a purposeful web app for a real audience. They apply technical skills, human-centered design, and AI literacy while making transparent, ethical choices. 


**Final Product Type:** Complete Web Application (with API integration, documentation, and reflection)

**When Project Begins:** Final two weeks of the semester (full duration of Unit 6)

---

## Sample project

<img src="https://images.code.org/9edc00ade8d52bae08a5de8c16d7372d-image-1776696508445.png" alt="sample explore-style app with grid of cards and detail view" width="750px" style="display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; border-radius:10px;"><br>

---

## What success looks like

> #### **By the end, students will:**
> - #### Design a clear, engaging homepage that communicates the purpose of their project
> - #### Organize content into meaningful sections that support user understanding
> - #### Show evidence of planning and iteration by refining their design over time
> - #### Make intentional design decisions and clearly explain their reasoning
> - #### Reflect on tradeoffs and how their choices impact usability and clarity

